{
  "id": "xujucyd",
  "title": "Chapter 10: Data Representation",
  "order": 10,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e9x3xi7",
      "content": "Data representation refers to the methods used to represent information inside a computer system. Computers work with binary data (0 and 1), so all forms of data such as numbers, text, images, and audio must be converted into binary form before processing."
    },
