    {
      "id": "s0cwwrt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.1.1 Binary Number System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bbuvict",
      "content": "The binary number system is the most important number system in computers. It uses only two digits: 0 and 1. Each digit is called a bit (binary digit)."
    },
    {
      "id": "zpwnbuo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.1.2 Octal Number System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mp0inym",
      "content": "The octal number system has base 8 and uses digits from 0 to 7."
    },
    {
      "id": "ly6adg0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.1.3 Decimal Number System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iz2r0oa",
      "content": "The decimal number system has base 10 and uses digits from 0 to 9."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "ASCII (American Standard Code for Information Interchange)",
      "id": "zxftfmg"
    },
    {
      "id": "snl0gie",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.1.4 Hexadecimal Number System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fjjyqt5",
      "content": "The hexadecimal number system has base 16 and uses digits 0–9 and letters A–F."
    },
    {
      "id": "xijeagq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.2 Binary Conversions"
    },
    {
      "id": "gdrwa5b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.2.1 Decimal to Binary Conversion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vgx8vpv",
      "content": "To convert decimal numbers to binary, repeatedly divide the number by 2 and record the remainders."
    },
    {
