    {
      "id": "w48ak21",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.2.2 Binary to Decimal Conversion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jt71fw2",
      "content": "Multiply each binary digit by powers of 2 and add the results."
    },
    {
      "id": "81d3u2s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.2.3 Binary to Octal Conversion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k7vxf24",
      "content": "Group binary digits into sets of three bits from right to left."
    },
    {
      "id": "94gxq5z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10.2.4 Binary to Hexadecimal Conversion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yybvkvr",
      "content": "Group binary digits into sets of four bits from right to left."
    },
    {
      "id": "on3uxep",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.3 ASCII (American Standard Code for Information Interchange)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0dspfn4",
      "content": "ASCII is a character encoding standard used to represent text in computers."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "In Hexadecimal system, letter A represents decimal 10, B represents 11, up to F representing 15.",
        "To convert Binary to Octal, group binary digits into groups of 3 bits from right to left.",
        "To convert Binary to Hexadecimal, group binary digits into groups of 4 bits from right to left.",
        "Standard 7-bit ASCII can represent up to 128 unique characters (2^7)."
      ],
      "id": "xzyd4we"
    },
